      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T08:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e and iiuc it should not avoid to manage this CRAS call.\n\nCould you please tell why?\n\nEvery telephony operation should not affect the CRAS-source call. The call should be added/removed on and only on SCO connected/disconnected.\n\nHi @whalechang@google.com, if I recall correctly, what we expect when hanging up a call is:\n1. Floss updates the call list and propagates the event to App and Headset\n2. App stops using audio\n3. CRAS cleans up the SCO\n4. Floss removes the CRAS call\n\nIs that correct?",
      "parentUuid": "7c91ce6a_24799713",
